  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the border-crossing scene as the target of political action",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the border-crossing scene (border_crossing_scene) as the recipient of the political framing presented in the text. The meme positions the viewer as someone who perceives the migrants as 'those who have no right to be here,' and thus the user is aligned with the perspective that Democrats are 'giving rights' to them, which is framed as a negative or unfair action. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the emotional and political framing of the scene and text invites the user to identify with the viewpoint that immigration policy is a zero-sum game, making the user a passive recipient of this projection.",
